          %h3#cwcomplex_structure CW-complex structure
          #CWComplexStructure.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The real Grassmannians
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Gr
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gr_n(\mathbb{R}^k)
              and the complex Grassmannians
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Gr
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gr_n(\mathbb{C}^k)
              admit the structure of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complexes"} CW-complexes
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Gr
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi Gr
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Gr_n(\mathbb{R}^k)
                    \\hookrightarrow
                    Gr_n(\mathbb{R}^{k+1})
            %p
              are subcomplex incusion (hence
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+cell+complex"} relative cell complex
              inclusions).
            %p
              Accordingly there is an induced CW-complex structure on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %munder
                        %mi lim
                        %mo ⟶
                      %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mi Gr
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    B O(n) \simeq \underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim}_k Gr_n(\mathbb{R}^k)
                    \\,.
          %p
            A proof is spelled out in (
            %a{:href => "#Hatcher"}> Hatcher, section 1.2 (pages 31-34)
            ).
          %p
